# Claim: a file handle a pattern binds out of a call's Result or Option and closes in the arm with `close(^name)` or `consume(^name)` closes exactly once, whether the arm falls through to the match's end or returns out of a loop, on o0, o1 and o2 (the artifact store lock's shape; a second close hung `jet self doctor`).
# Hand-derived: each round writes "round N" (7 bytes) into a fresh file and reads it back, and "leaked" is the process's open descriptor count minus the count before the first round, so 0 means every handle closed; "return text" is the file the returning arm wrote.
fixture: handle_matched_out_of_a_call_result_closes_once.fixture
env: NO_COLOR=1
env: JET_STORE_DIR={work}/cache
step: jet run --allow=FS.Read,FS.Write -O0 run.jet
exit: 0 # o0
stdout: = handle_matched_out_of_a_call_result_closes_once.out # o0
step: jet run --allow=FS.Read,FS.Write -O1 run.jet
exit: 0 # o1
stdout: = handle_matched_out_of_a_call_result_closes_once.out # o1
step: jet run --allow=FS.Read,FS.Write -O2 run.jet
exit: 0 # o2
stdout: = handle_matched_out_of_a_call_result_closes_once.out # o2
